From b4161bca82d2745c26ffc7bf7ddfc43273227a62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 13:42:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 113/113] DOS-PORT: patch 0113 -- rebuild the light table only
 when its inputs change

create_light_table() is 1351 ms on HW-486-66 (patch 0109's brackets):
255*256 = 65,280 bestfit_color() calls, each a scan of the palette. It
runs on EVERY load_new_room(), because ac/room.cpp nulls color_map
immediately before calling generate_light_table(), defeating that
function's own guard. So it is paid at every room transition during play
and at every save restore (game/savegame.cpp:834), not only at startup --
a hitch the player feels at a door, not just a load cost.

room.cpp's null is deliberately NOT removed: it is what discards a
blender a script may have set, so removing it would change behaviour.
Only the redundant rebuild is skipped. maincoltable is written by nothing
except the create_light_table() call here, so a table built earlier is
still intact when it is reused.

The cache key is every input create_light_table() actually branches on:
the 256-entry palette AND whether rgb_map is set. With rgb_map non-null
it takes a different branch (libsrc/allegro/src/color.c:765) and produces
a different table from the same palette, and ac/room.cpp:854 sets rgb_map
for games with anti-aliased sprites -- so keying on the palette alone
would have been a real correctness bug.

Byte-identity is measured rather than argued: with patch 0111's
DOSAGS_LIGHTTABLE_VERIFY=1, a rebuild on an unchanged palette memcmp'd
equal across all 65,536 entries on the bench8 full scene.

Scope, stated plainly: this cannot touch the FIRST build, so it does
nothing for a single-room benchmark and nothing for Gate 1. The saving is
entirely on the second and later calls.
---
 Engine/ac/region.cpp | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 55 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Engine/ac/region.cpp b/Engine/ac/region.cpp
index e32e5fdb1..9e128b387 100644
--- a/Engine/ac/region.cpp
+++ b/Engine/ac/region.cpp
@@ -195,6 +195,61 @@ void generate_light_table()
         }
 #endif
 #ifdef __DJGPP__
+        // DOS-PORT patch 0113: rebuild only when the inputs changed.
+        //
+        // create_light_table() is 1351 ms on HW-486-66 (patch 0109's
+        // brackets): 255*256 = 65,280 bestfit_color() calls, each a scan
+        // of the palette. It runs on EVERY load_new_room(), because
+        // ac/room.cpp nulls color_map immediately before calling this,
+        // which defeats the guard above -- so it is paid at every room
+        // transition and every save restore (game/savegame.cpp:834), not
+        // just at startup.
+        //
+        // room.cpp's null is NOT removed: it is what discards a blender a
+        // script may have set. Only the redundant rebuild is skipped, and
+        // maincoltable is written by nothing but the call below, so a
+        // table built earlier is still intact when reused.
+        //
+        // The key is every input create_light_table() branches on: the
+        // 256-entry palette AND whether rgb_map is set. With rgb_map
+        // non-null it takes a different branch
+        // (libsrc/allegro/src/color.c:765) and produces a DIFFERENT table
+        // from the same palette; ac/room.cpp:854 sets rgb_map for games
+        // with anti-aliased sprites, so keying on the palette alone would
+        // be a real correctness bug, not a theoretical one.
+        //
+        // Byte-identity is measured, not argued: with patch 0111's
+        // DOSAGS_LIGHTTABLE_VERIFY=1 a rebuild on an unchanged palette
+        // memcmp'd equal across all 65,536 entries (bench8 full scene).
+        {
+            static unsigned char dp_pal[768];
+            static bool dp_pal_valid = false;
+            static bool dp_had_rgb_map = false;
+            const uclock_t _dp_lt_skip = uclock();
+            unsigned char cur[768];
+            for (int i = 0; i < 256; i++)
+            {
+                cur[i * 3 + 0] = (unsigned char)palette[i].r;
+                cur[i * 3 + 1] = (unsigned char)palette[i].g;
+                cur[i * 3 + 2] = (unsigned char)palette[i].b;
+            }
+            const bool has_rgb_map = (rgb_map != nullptr);
+            if (dp_pal_valid && has_rgb_map == dp_had_rgb_map &&
+                memcmp(cur, dp_pal, sizeof(dp_pal)) == 0)
+            {
+                dos_port_startup_timing.lighttable_reused++;
+                debug_script_log("DOSAGS_LIGHTTABLE call=%ld action=reused ms=%ld reused_total=%ld",
+                                 dos_port_startup_timing.lighttable_rebuilt +
+                                     dos_port_startup_timing.lighttable_reused,
+                                 (long)((uclock() - _dp_lt_skip) * 1000 / UCLOCKS_PER_SEC),
+                                 dos_port_startup_timing.lighttable_reused);
+                color_map = &maincoltable;
+                return;
+            }
+            memcpy(dp_pal, cur, sizeof(dp_pal));
+            dp_pal_valid = true;
+            dp_had_rgb_map = has_rgb_map;
+        }
         // DOS-PORT patch 0112: time EVERY generate_light_table() call.
         // Measurement only; the table is still rebuilt unconditionally.
         //
